{
  "method": "Compare BMFToolkit bones with the Denver VHF bones of the same donor, bone by bone, without shipping them.\n\nBMFToolkit (Sreenivasa & Gonzalez-Alvarado, zlib LICENSE at the repository root) contains lower-body\nbone meshes extracted from the Visible Human Female CT: right-side bones segmented, left side mirrored,\nsacrum symmetrized, neutral-pose corrected and smoothed. Denver VHF bones come from the cryosections of\nthe same donor. Because the two sets are in different poses and frames, every bone is aligned by a\nrigid ICP (no scale) before measuring surface distances; the recorded transform is a comparison aid,\nnot a composition transform. Output: generated/bmftoolkit-comparison.json.",
  "not_shipped": true,
  "licence_evidence": {
    "repository_license_file": "sources/BMFToolkit/LICENSE (zlib licence text; \"this software\"; no separate data terms; the data folder is part of the same distribution)",
    "zenodo_record": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.889060 (license id other-open, access open)",
    "github_api_license": "NOASSERTION (non-standard licence header)",
    "position": "zlib is permissive and OSI-approved, but its text addresses software; whether the authors intend it to cover the mesh data is not stated. Meshes stay out of the shipped atlases until the authors confirm; see docs/LICENSING.md for the prepared request."
